filex-office-editor (scripts/x2t), BRF Tech, 2026-10-16: the per-pixel loops
of CxImage's PNG encoder and decoder for an image with an alpha channel move
out of Encode and Decode into three helpers of their own, unchanged, kept
out of line (DesktopEditor/cximage/CxImage/ximapng.cpp, ximapng.h).

Built with emscripten (SUPPORT_LONGJMP=emscripten), every call made from a
function that calls setjmp goes through an invoke_<sig> wrapper - in the
page a JavaScript function with a try/catch, on a server a call out of the
module to the host and back - and Encode and Decode call setjmp (libpng's
error handling). So a picture of N pixels made about 2N such calls:
BlindGetPixelColor and AlphaGet for every pixel written, AlphaSet for every
pixel read.

Measured (2026-10-16, Bug61268.doc, 509 pictures - EMF ones the editor gets
as SVG and PNG - into the editor's format): 145,265,861 invoke_* calls
before, 374,924 after; the server build under wazero 37-38 s before, 18.7-20
s after; the page's x2t in Node 12.3-13 s before, 10.0-10.2 s after (the
Document Server: 10.4 s). The Editor.bin, every PNG and every PDF of the
measurement set come out the same as before (the PDFs but their dates).

git apply reads from the first "diff --git" line on.

